WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
LOCKS

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.440
Tsukasa... What are you doing here?

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.400
You mean you haven't heard
anything from Mr. Katsuragi?

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.950
No... I just...

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.120
asked him where I could find Satoru.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.830
Satoru is not at the hotel right now.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.830
I'll take you to him.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.040
Just take us back toward Tokyo.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.090
I think this is my first time
in a car with you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.600
-It is?
-Yes, I'm sure it is!

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.440
Don't forget, you only got your license
after Satoru started living with you.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.980
That made me want to get one too.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.530
But when I asked the CEO,
he just laughed at me.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.780
'Cause I was only
13 years old at the time!

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.410
-I was too...
-Tsukasa.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.370
Even if you are taking me to Satoru,
I won't be allowed to see him, will I?

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.120
Definitely not.
He's under close surveillance.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.590
What's more, this car's movements are
being tracked, you realize?

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.840
All Company employees' cars are.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.180
But that's why you picked this car, isn't it?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.390
So that you could use it as a decoy
by getting someone else to drive it.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:08.980
You really do know how to play
the Company at its own game!

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.520
You were the one who showed Satoru
how to handle the lookouts too, right?

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.780
I have to admit, I had no idea that
you'd been watching our movements.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.570
You really are amazing, Mr. Hayashi.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.830
But I suppose letting me into your car
was your one big mistake.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.290
Why would you let that happen?

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.120
Did you meet Meiling?

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.630
Meiling.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.050
Drop us off out front.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.980
Yes, I saw her.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.060
That has to be your greatest masterpiece.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:02.400
Masterpiece my ass! The kid was taken away
before she was able to create a lock!

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.410
She'll never be able to have
a normal life like that!

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.620
And therein lies the masterpiece.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.710
You made her into a pet
that will be loyal forever!

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:16.590
Did you know that she's so obedient
that everyone calls her "baby"?

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.760
I didn't show her how to use an image
so that she could be turned into a puppet!

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.470
The Company told me I had to
make a choice.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.510
Either I continue making puppets
for them, or I crush Satoru.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.520
So you're planning on making
a run for it with Satoru?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.860
Because I found Satoru,

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.190
his parents were killed.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.860
Now I have to protect him, at all costs.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.490
Is Satoru doing all right?

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.080
I see.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.750
So you really don't care about me at all.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:59.040
You'd happily turn the Company into
your enemy to protect Satoru.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.590
But you don't even think to ask me
how I've been all this time.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.010
Tsukasa...

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.760
You know, Mr. Hayashi...

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.140
I always expected you'd come back.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.100
I thought that once Satoru
had proved himself,

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:17.190
you and I could get back
to working together.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:21.650
Believing in that possibility made me
strive to become the best.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.610
But now... you want to run away?

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.990
Why would you do that...?

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.580
As a result, now I've been told
to crush you.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.340
If I do that, the CEO is going to
make me his son.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.840
What do you think of that?
I'll finally be a Company executive.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:54.470
And it's all thanks to you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:58.060
All because of your selfish attempt
to escape...

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.440
Why couldn't you just keep making
"babies" for them?

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.820
It's not like we're on the side
of justice!

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.700
You really don't get it do you, Tsukasa!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.830
I didn't share my peak
to create a bunch of pawns!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.080
That goes for both you and Satoru, too.
All I wanted to do was help you!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.830
And that was your biggest mistake.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:25.090
You get carried away and share your peak
with whomever takes your fancy.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.720
But you don't know what effect that has.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:35.600
That's because you've never experienced
someone sharing their peak with you.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.940
So you can't possibly understand
how forever indebted to you

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.980
such a person feels.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:46.740
If you hadn't shared your peak with us,

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.740
what would've happened to me?
Or to Satoru?

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:54.080
I expect he would've met
the same fate I was facing.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.500
Just thinking about it
is terrifying enough.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.380
Do you have any idea how important you are
to someone who has felt that way?

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:06.050
You are everything to us!

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.930
And being someone's everything
can be very dangerous...

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.680
Gin and tonic...

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.560
Uh, but use cola instead of tonic.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.140
Certainly, sir.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:25.020
Oh, so you're an adult then?

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.820
A martini for me.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:30.570
And put his drink on my bar tab.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.200
I'll treat you.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:38.450
Hey. Put this lady's drink on my tab.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.790
How gentlemanly, for a such a young man.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.250
When you look like this,

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:48.590
you get used to flirtatious women
poking fun at you.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.720
Who said I was poking fun at you?

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.550
Hey. To our good health.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.390
Oops!

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.060
You okay?

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.730
Y...Yeah.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.990
How lucky your clothes didn't get wet.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.240
You're right. Very lucky...

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:17.030
I think I might be drunk.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.490
How about you? You feeling tipsy?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:24.750
You can lean on me if you need to.
You'll feel better if you do.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.380
Okay. In that case...

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.640
How about we go get a little crazy?

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.140
Is this how you have your fun?
Doesn't it make you feel empty inside?

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.890
Who the hell are you?

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:48.520
It's a pleasure to meet you, Satoru.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.280
I've heard all about you from Mr. Hayashi.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:56.160
Mr. Hayashi? You met with him?

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.660
Is he well? Where is he now?

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.540
I met with him in Beijing.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:05.670
He had his passport on him when he left
so I expected he'd be abroad.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.750
So, you did some work with him?

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.920
I did. But I'm not an image user...

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:16.260
Say, shall we go somewhere more private?

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.310
-We're using the room in the back.
-Err... I'm afraid that's for...

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:24.390
Relax. I'm staying in the suite upstairs!

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.190
Oh, in that case go ahead.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.310
There are more rooms upstairs...?

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.190
Our bond is far too strong.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:38.700
If such a bond spreads any further,
it may become a threat to the Company.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:43.950
That's why I asked them to keep
Meiling away from you.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.460
I told them that to stop a bond forming,

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.790
she couldn't be allowed
to have a personality.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:54.760
How could you say something so awful!

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:56.800
What's so awful about it?

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:01.140
You were the one who said I should work
for the Company, weren't you?

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:10.270
Seriously...
Do I have to spell it all out for them?

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.520
I guess it can't be helped.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.900
The owner of this place is
a Company employee,

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:20.320
but even he only knows that
the VIP floor security guards

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.620
and the trainee staff are lookouts.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.080
He hasn't been told anything about
what the other departments do,

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:30.130
certainly not something top secret
like the existence of "crushers".

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:34.250
And are you a Company employee
or a crusher?

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.340
I am both.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.010
Call me Jin.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.010
Okay. So, are you here
to give me an assignment?

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:46.140
Nope. I just wanted to have a chat.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:50.980
Would you mind showing me
your cell phone?

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:54.610
If you really are a Company employee,
you'll have Mr. Katsuragi's number.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.690
Do I really look that suspicious?

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.870
Why would a Company employee
talk to me about lookouts?

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:04.990
Here you go.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.170
And what did you want
to chat about exactly?

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:14.460
Could it be about me sneaking out
of the hotel?

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:16.300
You're terrible, you know.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.050
I've known Mr. Hayashi for longer
than you have, you realize?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.050
Huh?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.800
You're kidding...

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:28.730
-This is tedious. Are you even listening?
-I met him 12 years ago.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.270
So if she's about 25 now, she can't have
even been 13 when she met him.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.690
Can you even become
 an employee at that age?

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:39.740
All I know about the Company
is what I need to know for my work.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:44.570
I only recently found out that there are
other people who can use an image, too.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.330
I suppose that's how the Company
likes to keep things.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.000
The Company's doing all it can
to ensure image users aren't exposed.

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:54.920
Surely Mr. Hayashi didn't teach her first?

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.210
This is news to me.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:00.380
After all, even if we have top class
IT security systems,

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:04.720
you're able to hack into the heads
of the people operating the computers.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.970
We can't have outsiders finding out
about our business...

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:11.640
But if she doesn't use an image, then...

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.480
Ah, I've got it!

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.730
You're Chinese, aren't you?
We can speak in Mandarin if you want.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:19.400
Oh, you can speak Chinese!

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.530
But Japanese is perfectly fine.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:23.860
-Don't worry about me.
-So, she's Chinese...

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.240
If they met when Mr. Hayashi was in China,

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.870
she would have been eight, or nine?

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.500
There's a reason the CEO is this cautious.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.670
There used to be some people...
You know...

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:41.010
people who could manipulate others
using hypnosis.

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:43.880
You mean the qigong masters?

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:46.260
Oh, you've heard of them?

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.220
Mr. Hayashi told me.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:52.020
He said he learned how to hypnotize
from those masters.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:56.770
That's right. And the boss of those qigong
masters was in fact the CEO's father.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.940
They spent years helping the mafia,

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:03.400
then the CEO gathered all the qigong
masters and started the Company.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:08.160
And the modern day "crushers" were taught
by those qigong masters, right?

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.660
You've got it.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.830
Even the CEO's younger sister became
a crusher thanks to them.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.250
That's right. She was
the first of the crushers.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.330
The first person Mr. Hayashi
 ever synced with.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.920
But one day,

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:24.470
a handful of the masters betrayed
and murdered the CEO's father.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.680
You're kidding!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.550
And after that,
 the Company went and killed

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.720
all of the qigong masters
and even their children.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.690
Satoru, you'll need to pretend you've
 never heard what I've told you.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:36.770
Why though?

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:41.650
Because there'd be no reason for someone
 who knows this to love the Company.

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:45.610
If they find out that you know,
they'll view you as a threat.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.780
You wouldn't want them to think
 you'd betray them, would you?

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:54.370
Not only that, all the crushers taught by
the qigong masters were also killed.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.120
Mr. Katsuragi was spared because
he was already an employee,

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:01.250
and Mr. Hayashi because he was
an image user.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:05.130
So, why is this woman still alive?

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:08.260
-Now, guess what...
-Could she be a relative of the CEO?

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.970
The one who tracked down the treacherous
qigong masters was Mr. Hayashi.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.390
The Company owes him
a great debt of gratitude.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.020
He didn't tell me that!

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.020
Well, I'll be...

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:24.150
I suppose he didn't want to say anything.
He might have known some of them I guess.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.530
I see. It's because he found them
that they were...

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.780
-That's not the only thing.
-But still, this woman...

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.950
What the hell is she talking
about this stuff for?

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:38.040
Why'd she decide to tell me
about the lookouts?

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.580
There's something real fishy about her.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.920
I'd dive in and take a look
 if she weren't a crusher...

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.590
Could she be lying about all this?

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:48.090
Wait, where'd she look just now?

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.680
This might just be an act.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.720
I could give her a glass
and take a look...

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:56.020
-How about another drink?
-How about another drink?

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.180
-Err...
-Err...

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.390
All I've done for the last 12 years

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.650
is follow the principle you taught me,
Mr. Hayashi!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.070
"Do as the Company wishes!"

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:10.400
Do you remember telling me that
the day you came back with Satoru?

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:15.120
And that we could no longer live together
because the Company said so.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:19.160
I went along with it,
because I had no choice!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:23.080
Because you told me to do so,
Mr. Hayashi!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:24.750
All I ever wanted was...

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:28.090
Tsukasa! Tsukasa!

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:32.260
It's okay. Come with me.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.890
We'll go together.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:42.730
No way! Were we both thinking
the same thing just now?

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:43.730
Huh?

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.190
Makes sense, seeing as we do similar work.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.240
It's natural to be wary since we've both
gone through the same sort of training.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.870
Why do you think I brought up
the subject of lookouts?

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:59.750
Do you think I don't know you manipulated
the lookouts so you could sneak out?

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:03.210
Ah, so that's what
this is about, after all...

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:04.500
Sorry 'bout that...

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.750
I'm not here to tell you off!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:14.010
Ugh... I can't keep it in any longer so
I'll just tell you. I'm the CEO's niece!

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.050
Oh... really?

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:17.390
I knew it!

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:23.140
And actually I was told to come and
ask you if you wouldn't like to join us.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:24.400
Huh?

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.270
Satoru. How would you like
to become a Company employee?

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.530
An employee... Me?

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:35.780
That's right. If you did, you'd be able to
come and go as you please.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.700
But, I have to...

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:41.080
ask Mr. Hayashi...

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.170
Why can't we live together?

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.050
I'm sorry, Tsukasa.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.670
There's nothing that can be done.
It's the Company's call.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:58.220
I've been told I can't raise both
you and Satoru together.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.970
You're a smart kid.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.770
Make sure you do as the Company says.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.810
Don't worry, I will.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.780
But don't forget one thing, Tsukasa.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:15.360
If you absolutely insist,

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:17.450
the three of us could live together.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:24.460
You never said that to me back then,
Mr. Hayashi.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.830
Are you seriously trying
to rewrite my memories?

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:30.840
-You're an asshole. This is uncalled for.
-That's not it, Tsukasa!

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.010
You want to pretend nothing ever happened,
and get me to cooperate?

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:38.890
That's not it at all!
I wanted you to know my true feelings.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.810
I wish I could redo it differently!

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.470
Redo it differently?

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.520
Just what is it that
you want to redo differently?

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:54.570
Redo how I stupidly went along with
everything you said for years?

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:56.950
Or how I believed that
you would be there at the end,

00:17:57.110 --> 00:18:00.410
as I worked tirelessly to infiltrate
the inner workings of the Company.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:01.870
Tsukasa...

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:05.250
Or perhaps how I failed
to reach your expectations

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.620
as an ally of justice?

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.460
There's no need to change anything.

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:16.050
All I need is to understand you
as you are now, Mr. Hayashi.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:19.510
But you know something...
That's impossible.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:23.140
I can't let go of what happened
just like that.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:26.890
You see, I now have a personality.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:30.900
I have a will of my own and memories
that are mine, just like everyone else.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:35.150
They are all gifts from you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.740
So, if you want to redo it all,

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:41.280
you'll first have to take back
the sympathy you extended

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.780
to a kid destined for organ harvesting.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:49.250
You'll have to restart from the time
you shared your peak with me.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:55.300
Your first mistake was to allow me
to have a personality.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:00.340
If you want to take back that mistake,
you'll have to crush me.

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.930
If you don't, more mistakes
are sure to follow.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:08.810
Lose me again and I will be sure
to crush Satoru the next chance I have.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:13.860
If you wish to protect Satoru,
you'll need to crush me.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.980
You know full well I can't crush you.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:20.610
In that case,
this will last until I crush you.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.870
You know you can't match my speed.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:28.370
Perhaps not, but I've increased
my repertoire quite a bit.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.120
Shit...

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:40.050
Hey. Don't let that one in.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.430
That's Hayashi's pet, am I right?

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.850
Unlike us, I hear they can even
alter people's memories.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.100
-Pet...?
-What? Don't worry about it.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:51.390
From now on, this one's my pet.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.360
I'll be training it more severely
than Hayashi ever did.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.240
Katsuragi, does your rank even
allow you to keep a pet?

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.740
Give it here.

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.370
Aren't you the lucky one?

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.660
If I hadn't made you my pet,

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:11.000
you'd have been harvested to replace
some old rich guy's body parts.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.460
What are you doing this time?

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.500
This is hardly the time to try
and mess with my memories.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.760
I'm going to take you with me, Tsukasa.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:24.260
Even if you don't want me to...

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.010
I see...

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:30.140
You really want to rewrite
my memories, don't you?

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.810
But you can't change my memories.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.110
Having a memory bank that
cannot be revised by anybody

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:40.440
is the one sliver of pride that a pet
such as myself can hold onto.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:45.280
To that end, I created
an incredibly strong lock.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:48.160
Of course, your lock.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.910
I'll have you show it to me.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:20:59.040
A lock?

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.170
That's right, Hiroki. A lock.

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:06.430
Create some valleys around your peak
and people will be scared to enter, right?

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:08.970
Why is it bad for people to come in?

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:11.220
You can't let anyone in, Hiroki!

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:14.230
No one else is allowed into your peak.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:19.020
If that happens, they could change
your memories or even erase them!

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.440
Huh...

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:25.780
So, basically, a lock is a valley you use
to hide and protect your peak.

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.200
So, this is your pet, Tsukasa?

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:34.040
That's right. My pet hates valleys,

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.040
which means his lock is pretty weak.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.550
Unlike him, I'm a lot more wary of others.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.090
My peak is locked tight.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:45.840
But you know, Tsukasa...

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:49.180
Using too strong of a lock

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:52.470
just makes it obvious that
something valuable is there.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.850
What's that dog there for?

00:21:57.310 --> 00:22:00.980
That dog is hiding your peak.
It is a part of your valley, am I right?

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:03.860
That dog is the entrance to your valley.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:09.620
I know where to find your valley, Tsukasa.

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:13.620
And I'm going to use it as
a point of entry to your peak.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
Artist: Ryotimo
